{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Additional production occurrence\n\nDuring parallel F17, F18, F29, and F31 documentation work at code base `ae4030bd4a920762e27971f59a7aafdc4fcc0026`, `rebar comment prosaic-radon-sardine` committed the F29 GREEN evidence locally but terminal push recovery failed. The remote rejected `HEAD -> tickets` because another session had advanced the ref. Rebar reported 17 unpushed local ticket commits and stated that the backlog grew. The command exited zero after adding the local comment, so the write was durable in the shared tracker clone but was not shared through `origin/tickets` as the concurrency contract requires.\n\nF31 recorded the matching stale-reference failure and a successful serialized control on this bug. The existing controlled proof also produced parallel failures and zero serialized failures. This occurrence therefore belongs to the confirmed common-directory coordination defect. No duplicate bug was created."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787530176287733001,"uuid":"6cf47982-5da1-49a9-b699-8c66afe9d621"}